    return [
        ['id'=>9300,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>324,'title'=>'Global Inflation Hits Jakarta as Beijing Supply Chain Disruption Worsens','exc'=>'Economic pressure and international isolation are beginning to take a toll, with the currency losing 10 percent of its value against the dollar in recent weeks.','body'=>'<p>Few anticipated the scale of what was about to unfold when the first reports emerged. Within hours, the story had drawn international attention and sparked a conversation that showed no signs of abating.</p><p>Experts who had been monitoring the area said the situation had been building for some time and that those with the clearest view had long warned that the status quo was unsustainable.</p><p>The response from institutions was cautious but pointed, with carefully worded statements that acknowledged the gravity of the situation without committing to specific action.</p><p>Looking ahead, the consensus among observers was that the coming weeks would be decisive, with outcomes likely to shape the landscape in this area for years to come.</p>','cat'=>'World News','author'=>'Priya Nair','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1529107386315-e1a2ed48a620?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Middle East','Oil','Conflict'],'date'=>'2022-06-28 18:02:00'],
        ['id'=>9301,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>133,'title'=>'Beijing Joins NATO After Decades-Long Application Process','exc'=>'A landmark agreement reached after 300 months of negotiations could reshape the geopolitical landscape of the region for a generation.','body'=>'<p>The story began quietly enough, in the margins of an event that had attracted little wider notice, but it quickly gathered momentum as more details came to light and more voices entered the conversation.</p><p>By the time the full extent of the matter became apparent, it had already begun to reshape perceptions and trigger a reappraisal of assumptions that had gone largely unchallenged for years.</p><p>Those who had been raising concerns for some time said they were relieved that the issue was finally receiving the attention it deserved, while cautioning that recognition was only a first step.</p><p>The road ahead will require sustained effort, adequate resources, and a willingness to have difficult conversations — all of which have historically proven harder to sustain than the initial burst of interest suggests.</p>','cat'=>'World News','author'=>'Ahmed Al-Rashid','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1504711434969-e33886168f5c?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Asia','Pacific','Relations'],'date'=>'2025-04-21 13:51:00'],
        ['id'=>9302,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>2897,'title'=>'Saudi Arabia Withdraws Ambassador from Brazil Over Espionage Row','exc'=>'World leaders expressed deep concern as the standoff entered its 8th week, with no sign of compromise from either side despite intensive mediation efforts.','body'=>'<p>The findings emerged from a process that had been years in the making, drawing on data, testimony, and analysis assembled painstakingly from dozens of independent sources.</p><p>Those involved described it as one of the most complex undertakings they had been part of, requiring sustained coordination across multiple disciplines, jurisdictions, and institutional cultures.</p><p>The significance of what had been uncovered was not lost on the participants, who were careful to present their conclusions in measured terms while making clear the weight of evidence behind them.</p><p>What comes next remains contested, but few doubted that the moment marked a turning point from which simple return to the previous state of affairs would be difficult, perhaps impossible.</p>','cat'=>'World News','author'=>'Priya Nair','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551009175-15bfef3ae1de?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['NATO','Alliance','Security'],'date'=>'2022-07-18 16:54:00'],
        ['id'=>9303,'published'=>true,'featured'=>true,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>649,'title'=>'Mass Graves Discovered in Bangladesh as Conflict Enters Third Year','exc'=>'The United Nations called for an immediate end to hostilities as civilian casualties mounted and aid agencies struggled to reach those most in need.','body'=>'<p>The developments unfolded rapidly over a 100-hour period, catching observers off guard and prompting urgent consultations among stakeholders who had been tracking the situation for weeks.</p><p>Sources familiar with the matter said that background discussions had been under way for some time, but that the speed of the final decision surprised even those closest to the process.</p><p>Reactions were swift. Analysts noted that the implications would likely reverberate well beyond the immediate context, touching on a range of related issues that had previously been treated as separate.</p><p>Officials declined to provide detailed comment, citing the sensitivity of ongoing processes, but indicated that further announcements were expected within days.</p>','cat'=>'World News','author'=>'Sophie Laurent','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1540910419892-4a36d2c3266c?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Africa','Development','Aid'],'date'=>'2024-01-11 11:45:00'],
        ['id'=>9304,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>1796,'title'=>'Ceasefire Agreement in Seoul Holds for Third Consecutive Day','exc'=>'A landmark agreement reached after 5 months of negotiations could reshape the geopolitical landscape of the region for a generation.','body'=>'<p>Numbers tell part of the story. The figures, released alongside a detailed technical appendix, showed trends that had been suspected but whose magnitude surprised even seasoned observers in the field.</p><p>Statisticians cautioned against over-interpretation of any single data point, noting that short-term fluctuations can obscure more fundamental patterns that only become visible over longer time horizons.</p><p>What the data could not capture, participants pointed out, was the human dimension — the lived experience of those whose circumstances were reflected in the rows and columns of the official record.</p><p>Further analysis is under way, and additional findings are expected to be published in the coming months as a fuller picture takes shape.</p>','cat'=>'World News','author'=>'Daniel Osei','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1573804633927-bfcbcd909acd?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Sanctions','Trade','Diplomacy'],'date'=>'2022-11-30 16:22:00'],
