        ['id'=>9372,'published'=>true,'featured'=>true,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>317,'title'=>'Ceasefire Agreement in Havana Holds for Third Consecutive Day','exc'=>'The United Nations called for an immediate end to hostilities as civilian casualties mounted and aid agencies struggled to reach those most in need.','body'=>'<p>The developments unfolded rapidly over a 200-hour period, catching observers off guard and prompting urgent consultations among stakeholders who had been tracking the situation for weeks.</p><p>Sources familiar with the matter said that background discussions had been under way for some time, but that the speed of the final decision surprised even those closest to the process.</p><p>Reactions were swift. Analysts noted that the implications would likely reverberate well beyond the immediate context, touching on a range of related issues that had previously been treated as separate.</p><p>Officials declined to provide detailed comment, citing the sensitivity of ongoing processes, but indicated that further announcements were expected within days.</p>','cat'=>'World News','author'=>'Priya Nair','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1529107386315-e1a2ed48a620?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Asia','Pacific','Relations'],'date'=>'2022-12-07 14:57:00'],
