        ['id'=>9562,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>2376,'title'=>'International Court Rules Against Addis Ababa in Landmark Judgement','exc'=>'Diplomats from 500 countries gathered as the security situation entered a critical phase, with international observers warning that failure to act could have far-reaching consequences.','body'=>'<p>Numbers tell part of the story. The figures, released alongside a detailed technical appendix, showed trends that had been suspected but whose magnitude surprised even seasoned observers in the field.</p><p>Statisticians cautioned against over-interpretation of any single data point, noting that short-term fluctuations can obscure more fundamental patterns that only become visible over longer time horizons.</p><p>What the data could not capture, participants pointed out, was the human dimension — the lived experience of those whose circumstances were reflected in the rows and columns of the official record.</p><p>Further analysis is under way, and additional findings are expected to be published in the coming months as a fuller picture takes shape.</p>','cat'=>'World News','author'=>'Marcus Webb','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1540910419892-4a36d2c3266c?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Diplomacy','Global','Conflict'],'date'=>'2023-11-23 14:19:00'],
