        ['id'=>10146,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>3611,'title'=>'Manufacturing Output Contracts for the IMF Consecutive Months','exc'=>'Investors reacted with cautious optimism as the company unveiled results that beat analyst forecasts by a wide margin, though concerns about longer-term growth persist.','body'=>'<p>Numbers tell part of the story. The figures, released alongside a detailed technical appendix, showed trends that had been suspected but whose magnitude surprised even seasoned observers in the field.</p><p>Statisticians cautioned against over-interpretation of any single data point, noting that short-term fluctuations can obscure more fundamental patterns that only become visible over longer time horizons.</p><p>What the data could not capture, participants pointed out, was the human dimension — the lived experience of those whose circumstances were reflected in the rows and columns of the official record.</p><p>Further analysis is under way, and additional findings are expected to be published in the coming months as a fuller picture takes shape.</p>','cat'=>'Business','author'=>'Rachel Kim','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1520333789090-1afc82db536a?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['GDP','Growth','Forecast'],'date'=>'2023-02-26 17:11:00'],
