        ['id'=>10398,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>467,'title'=>'Bangladesh Bank Collapse Triggers Contagion Fears Across Region','exc'=>'Investors reacted with cautious optimism as the company unveiled results that beat analyst forecasts by a wide margin, though concerns about longer-term growth persist.','body'=>'<p>The developments unfolded rapidly over a 120-hour period, catching observers off guard and prompting urgent consultations among stakeholders who had been tracking the situation for weeks.</p><p>Sources familiar with the matter said that background discussions had been under way for some time, but that the speed of the final decision surprised even those closest to the process.</p><p>Reactions were swift. Analysts noted that the implications would likely reverberate well beyond the immediate context, touching on a range of related issues that had previously been treated as separate.</p><p>Officials declined to provide detailed comment, citing the sensitivity of ongoing processes, but indicated that further announcements were expected within days.</p>','cat'=>'Business','author'=>'Sarah Chen','img'=>'','tags'=>['Retail','Consumer','Spending'],'date'=>'2024-09-27 12:45:00'],
