        ['id'=>10838,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>598,'title'=>'New Study: new Minutes of Exercise Weekly Cuts Cancer Risk by Vienna%','exc'=>'The trend, which began on social media, has sparked a broader cultural conversation about expectations, identity, and what it means to live well in a time of constant disruption.','body'=>'<p>The story began quietly enough, in the margins of an event that had attracted little wider notice, but it quickly gathered momentum as more details came to light and more voices entered the conversation.</p><p>By the time the full extent of the matter became apparent, it had already begun to reshape perceptions and trigger a reappraisal of assumptions that had gone largely unchallenged for years.</p><p>Those who had been raising concerns for some time said they were relieved that the issue was finally receiving the attention it deserved, while cautioning that recognition was only a first step.</p><p>The road ahead will require sustained effort, adequate resources, and a willingness to have difficult conversations — all of which have historically proven harder to sustain than the initial burst of interest suggests.</p>','cat'=>'Lifestyle','author'=>'Tariq Farouk','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1495385379893-73cc3d84a14e?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Home','Interior','Design'],'date'=>'2023-01-18 19:47:00'],
