        ['id'=>10864,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>1726,'title'=>'New Study: Turkey Minutes of Exercise Weekly Cuts Cancer Risk by Apple%','exc'=>'Researchers tracked 10 thousand participants over a decade, finding strong correlations between lifestyle choices and long-term health outcomes across all age groups studied.','body'=>'<p>Few anticipated the scale of what was about to unfold when the first reports emerged. Within hours, the story had drawn international attention and sparked a conversation that showed no signs of abating.</p><p>Experts who had been monitoring the area said the situation had been building for some time and that those with the clearest view had long warned that the status quo was unsustainable.</p><p>The response from institutions was cautious but pointed, with carefully worded statements that acknowledged the gravity of the situation without committing to specific action.</p><p>Looking ahead, the consensus among observers was that the coming weeks would be decisive, with outcomes likely to shape the landscape in this area for years to come.</p>','cat'=>'Lifestyle','author'=>'Tariq Farouk','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1498837167922-ddd27525d352?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Relationships','Family','Society'],'date'=>'2022-06-20 07:44:00'],
