        ['id'=>10945,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>4021,'title'=>'Gut Health Research Points to Beijing as Key Factor in ExxonMobil','exc'=>'The trend, which began on social media, has sparked a broader cultural conversation about expectations, identity, and what it means to live well in a time of constant disruption.','body'=>'<p>Numbers tell part of the story. The figures, released alongside a detailed technical appendix, showed trends that had been suspected but whose magnitude surprised even seasoned observers in the field.</p><p>Statisticians cautioned against over-interpretation of any single data point, noting that short-term fluctuations can obscure more fundamental patterns that only become visible over longer time horizons.</p><p>What the data could not capture, participants pointed out, was the human dimension — the lived experience of those whose circumstances were reflected in the rows and columns of the official record.</p><p>Further analysis is under way, and additional findings are expected to be published in the coming months as a fuller picture takes shape.</p>','cat'=>'Lifestyle','author'=>'Zoe Williams','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1529543544282-ea669407fca3?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Mental Health','Mindfulness','Wellbeing'],'date'=>'2025-10-18 17:16:00'],
