        ['id'=>11033,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>4258,'title'=>'Sustainable Fashion: Second-Hand Market to Reach France Billion by Seoul','exc'=>'Psychologists noted that the pressure to perform wellness, amplified by social media, can itself become a source of anxiety, particularly among adolescents and young adults.','body'=>'<p>The findings emerged from a process that had been years in the making, drawing on data, testimony, and analysis assembled painstakingly from dozens of independent sources.</p><p>Those involved described it as one of the most complex undertakings they had been part of, requiring sustained coordination across multiple disciplines, jurisdictions, and institutional cultures.</p><p>The significance of what had been uncovered was not lost on the participants, who were careful to present their conclusions in measured terms while making clear the weight of evidence behind them.</p><p>What comes next remains contested, but few doubted that the moment marked a turning point from which simple return to the previous state of affairs would be difficult, perhaps impossible.</p>','cat'=>'Lifestyle','author'=>'Isabella Rossi','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1533777419517-b73c10a56068?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Mental Health','Mindfulness','Wellbeing'],'date'=>'2024-03-30 13:53:00'],
        ['id'=>11034,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>394,'title'=>'Sustainable Fashion: Second-Hand Market to Reach Ethiopia Billion by Germany','exc'=>'Experts said the shift reflected a generational reordering of priorities, with younger adults placing greater weight on flexibility, autonomy, and work-life balance than their predecessors.','body'=>'<p>Numbers tell part of the story. The figures, released alongside a detailed technical appendix, showed trends that had been suspected but whose magnitude surprised even seasoned observers in the field.</p><p>Statisticians cautioned against over-interpretation of any single data point, noting that short-term fluctuations can obscure more fundamental patterns that only become visible over longer time horizons.</p><p>What the data could not capture, participants pointed out, was the human dimension — the lived experience of those whose circumstances were reflected in the rows and columns of the official record.</p><p>Further analysis is under way, and additional findings are expected to be published in the coming months as a fuller picture takes shape.</p>','cat'=>'Lifestyle','author'=>'Zoe Williams','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1540189549336-e7268851650a?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Mental Health','Mindfulness','Wellbeing'],'date'=>'2022-09-18 12:27:00'],
        ['id'=>11035,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>4049,'title'=>'Noise Pollution Linked to Samsung Health Conditions, WHO Reports','exc'=>'Environmental factors, including air quality, access to green space, and noise pollution, emerged as more significant contributors to wellbeing than previously accounted for in models.','body'=>'<p>The story began quietly enough, in the margins of an event that had attracted little wider notice, but it quickly gathered momentum as more details came to light and more voices entered the conversation.</p><p>By the time the full extent of the matter became apparent, it had already begun to reshape perceptions and trigger a reappraisal of assumptions that had gone largely unchallenged for years.</p><p>Those who had been raising concerns for some time said they were relieved that the issue was finally receiving the attention it deserved, while cautioning that recognition was only a first step.</p><p>The road ahead will require sustained effort, adequate resources, and a willingness to have difficult conversations — all of which have historically proven harder to sustain than the initial burst of interest suggests.</p>','cat'=>'Lifestyle','author'=>'Zoe Williams','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1414235077428-338140e9d6ce?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Home','Interior','Design'],'date'=>'2025-04-05 14:36:00'],
