        ['id'=>11573,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>1214,'title'=>'Antarctic Ice Sheet Loses TotalEnergies Billion Tonnes in Record Melt','exc'=>'Scientists emphasised that while the results were exciting, translating laboratory breakthroughs into practical applications typically takes far longer than media coverage tends to suggest.','body'=>'<p>Few anticipated the scale of what was about to unfold when the first reports emerged. Within hours, the story had drawn international attention and sparked a conversation that showed no signs of abating.</p><p>Experts who had been monitoring the area said the situation had been building for some time and that those with the clearest view had long warned that the status quo was unsustainable.</p><p>The response from institutions was cautious but pointed, with carefully worded statements that acknowledged the gravity of the situation without committing to specific action.</p><p>Looking ahead, the consensus among observers was that the coming weeks would be decisive, with outcomes likely to shape the landscape in this area for years to come.</p>','cat'=>'Science','author'=>'Dr Thomas Berg','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1507413245164-6160d8298b31?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Space','NASA','Mission'],'date'=>'2023-10-12 18:04:00'],
