        ['id'=>11575,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>4231,'title'=>'Solar Storm Warning: Largest Event in Vienna Years Could Hit Earth','exc'=>'Independent experts who reviewed the methodology praised its rigour while flagging several assumptions in the modelling that they said warranted further investigation.','body'=>'<p>The findings emerged from a process that had been years in the making, drawing on data, testimony, and analysis assembled painstakingly from dozens of independent sources.</p><p>Those involved described it as one of the most complex undertakings they had been part of, requiring sustained coordination across multiple disciplines, jurisdictions, and institutional cultures.</p><p>The significance of what had been uncovered was not lost on the participants, who were careful to present their conclusions in measured terms while making clear the weight of evidence behind them.</p><p>What comes next remains contested, but few doubted that the moment marked a turning point from which simple return to the previous state of affairs would be difficult, perhaps impossible.</p>','cat'=>'Science','author'=>'Dr Priya Kapoor','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1564325724739-bae0bd08762c?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Physics','Particle','CERN'],'date'=>'2024-06-12 12:27:00'],
        ['id'=>11576,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>634,'title'=>'Drought Linked to Nairobi Conflict Escalation, Climate Study Finds','exc'=>'Data collected over 40 decades by research stations on six continents formed the basis of the analysis, giving it an unprecedented scope in terms of geographic coverage.','body'=>'<p>Numbers tell part of the story. The figures, released alongside a detailed technical appendix, showed trends that had been suspected but whose magnitude surprised even seasoned observers in the field.</p><p>Statisticians cautioned against over-interpretation of any single data point, noting that short-term fluctuations can obscure more fundamental patterns that only become visible over longer time horizons.</p><p>What the data could not capture, participants pointed out, was the human dimension — the lived experience of those whose circumstances were reflected in the rows and columns of the official record.</p><p>Further analysis is under way, and additional findings are expected to be published in the coming months as a fuller picture takes shape.</p>','cat'=>'Science','author'=>'Dr Sarah Mitchell','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1446776899648-aa78eefe8ed0?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Climate','Carbon','Emissions'],'date'=>'2022-10-29 12:50:00'],
