        ['id'=>11647,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>3836,'title'=>'Microplastics Discovered in Human Poland for First Time','exc'=>'Independent experts who reviewed the methodology praised its rigour while flagging several assumptions in the modelling that they said warranted further investigation.','body'=>'<p>The findings emerged from a process that had been years in the making, drawing on data, testimony, and analysis assembled painstakingly from dozens of independent sources.</p><p>Those involved described it as one of the most complex undertakings they had been part of, requiring sustained coordination across multiple disciplines, jurisdictions, and institutional cultures.</p><p>The significance of what had been uncovered was not lost on the participants, who were careful to present their conclusions in measured terms while making clear the weight of evidence behind them.</p><p>What comes next remains contested, but few doubted that the moment marked a turning point from which simple return to the previous state of affairs would be difficult, perhaps impossible.</p>','cat'=>'Science','author'=>'Dr Priya Kapoor','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1564325724739-bae0bd08762c?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Space','NASA','Mission'],'date'=>'2022-07-10 11:15:00'],
        ['id'=>11648,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>true,'views'=>3166,'title'=>'Solar Storm Warning: Largest Event in South Africa Years Could Hit Earth','exc'=>'Data collected over 500 decades by research stations on six continents formed the basis of the analysis, giving it an unprecedented scope in terms of geographic coverage.','body'=>'<p>The story began quietly enough, in the margins of an event that had attracted little wider notice, but it quickly gathered momentum as more details came to light and more voices entered the conversation.</p><p>By the time the full extent of the matter became apparent, it had already begun to reshape perceptions and trigger a reappraisal of assumptions that had gone largely unchallenged for years.</p><p>Those who had been raising concerns for some time said they were relieved that the issue was finally receiving the attention it deserved, while cautioning that recognition was only a first step.</p><p>The road ahead will require sustained effort, adequate resources, and a willingness to have difficult conversations — all of which have historically proven harder to sustain than the initial burst of interest suggests.</p>','cat'=>'Science','author'=>'Dr Yuki Sato','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1446776899648-aa78eefe8ed0?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Medicine','Vaccine','Trial'],'date'=>'2024-02-16 22:07:00'],
