        ['id'=>11670,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>3623,'title'=>'Drought Linked to Goldman Sachs Conflict Escalation, Climate Study Finds','exc'=>'Scientists emphasised that while the results were exciting, translating laboratory breakthroughs into practical applications typically takes far longer than media coverage tends to suggest.','body'=>'<p>Few anticipated the scale of what was about to unfold when the first reports emerged. Within hours, the story had drawn international attention and sparked a conversation that showed no signs of abating.</p><p>Experts who had been monitoring the area said the situation had been building for some time and that those with the clearest view had long warned that the status quo was unsustainable.</p><p>The response from institutions was cautious but pointed, with carefully worded statements that acknowledged the gravity of the situation without committing to specific action.</p><p>Looking ahead, the consensus among observers was that the coming weeks would be decisive, with outcomes likely to shape the landscape in this area for years to come.</p>','cat'=>'Science','author'=>'Dr Priya Kapoor','img'=>'','tags'=>['Climate','Carbon','Emissions'],'date'=>'2022-02-04 11:55:00'],
        ['id'=>11671,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>3940,'title'=>'Microplastics Discovered in Human Kenya for First Time','exc'=>'Scientists emphasised that while the results were exciting, translating laboratory breakthroughs into practical applications typically takes far longer than media coverage tends to suggest.','body'=>'<p>Numbers tell part of the story. The figures, released alongside a detailed technical appendix, showed trends that had been suspected but whose magnitude surprised even seasoned observers in the field.</p><p>Statisticians cautioned against over-interpretation of any single data point, noting that short-term fluctuations can obscure more fundamental patterns that only become visible over longer time horizons.</p><p>What the data could not capture, participants pointed out, was the human dimension — the lived experience of those whose circumstances were reflected in the rows and columns of the official record.</p><p>Further analysis is under way, and additional findings are expected to be published in the coming months as a fuller picture takes shape.</p>','cat'=>'Science','author'=>'Dr Thomas Berg','img'=>'','tags'=>['Genetics','DNA','Breakthrough'],'date'=>'2025-09-20 15:11:00'],
