        ['id'=>11749,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>1011,'title'=>'South Korea Prime Minister Calls Snap Election Amid Economic Crisis','exc'=>'The vote was closer than many had expected, underscoring the deep polarisation of an electorate that appears to have lost confidence in both the governing party and the main alternative.','body'=>'<p>Numbers tell part of the story. The figures, released alongside a detailed technical appendix, showed trends that had been suspected but whose magnitude surprised even seasoned observers in the field.</p><p>Statisticians cautioned against over-interpretation of any single data point, noting that short-term fluctuations can obscure more fundamental patterns that only become visible over longer time horizons.</p><p>What the data could not capture, participants pointed out, was the human dimension — the lived experience of those whose circumstances were reflected in the rows and columns of the official record.</p><p>Further analysis is under way, and additional findings are expected to be published in the coming months as a fuller picture takes shape.</p>','cat'=>'Politics','author'=>'Brendan Walsh','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1540910419892-4a36d2c3266c?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Protest','Civil Rights','Movement'],'date'=>'2025-08-07 16:48:00'],
