        ['id'=>11752,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>4322,'title'=>'Coalition Government Collapses in Japan After Lima Defects','exc'=>'Voters interviewed outside polling stations described a profound sense of disillusionment with mainstream parties, citing broken promises and a growing disconnect from everyday concerns.','body'=>'<p>The story began quietly enough, in the margins of an event that had attracted little wider notice, but it quickly gathered momentum as more details came to light and more voices entered the conversation.</p><p>By the time the full extent of the matter became apparent, it had already begun to reshape perceptions and trigger a reappraisal of assumptions that had gone largely unchallenged for years.</p><p>Those who had been raising concerns for some time said they were relieved that the issue was finally receiving the attention it deserved, while cautioning that recognition was only a first step.</p><p>The road ahead will require sustained effort, adequate resources, and a willingness to have difficult conversations — all of which have historically proven harder to sustain than the initial burst of interest suggests.</p>','cat'=>'Politics','author'=>'Mara Lindqvist','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1476514525535-07fb3b4ae5f1?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Protest','Civil Rights','Movement'],'date'=>'2024-07-24 19:58:00'],
