        ['id'=>11771,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>3376,'title'=>'Election Fraud Allegations Spark Protests in Philippines Capital','exc'=>'The revelations triggered calls for a full independent inquiry, with whistleblowers alleging that senior officials had been aware of the problem but chose not to act for political reasons.','body'=>'<p>Numbers tell part of the story. The figures, released alongside a detailed technical appendix, showed trends that had been suspected but whose magnitude surprised even seasoned observers in the field.</p><p>Statisticians cautioned against over-interpretation of any single data point, noting that short-term fluctuations can obscure more fundamental patterns that only become visible over longer time horizons.</p><p>What the data could not capture, participants pointed out, was the human dimension — the lived experience of those whose circumstances were reflected in the rows and columns of the official record.</p><p>Further analysis is under way, and additional findings are expected to be published in the coming months as a fuller picture takes shape.</p>','cat'=>'Politics','author'=>'Hassan El-Amin','img'=>'','tags'=>['Protest','Civil Rights','Movement'],'date'=>'2022-05-01 11:30:00'],
